{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsKnots.LinearJSJVolume","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.LinearJSJVolume","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.vol_neutron_increment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.vol_neutron_increment","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L106-L113","doc":"**Neutron increment.** Each added neutron contributes exactly `Vol_n`.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.vol_proton_increment","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.vol_proton_increment","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L96-L104","doc":"**Proton increment.** Each added proton contributes exactly `Vol_p`: the\ndiscrete `Z`-derivative of the atomic volume is the constant `Vol_p`.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.atomic_volume_additive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.atomic_volume_additive","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L82-L94","doc":"**Cluster additivity.** Combining two nucleon clusters adds their volumes\n(hence, under the mass functor, the *leading* `m_qCLT_approx` masses).\nA genuine consequence of the decomposition hypothesis — this is the\nstructural content the `m_qCLT_approx` channel relies on, not a restatement\nof the hypothesis.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.JSJ_volume_additivity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.JSJ_volume_additivity","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L77-L80","doc":"The linear law, conditional on the decomposition hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.AtomicJSJDecomposition.volume_linear","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.AtomicJSJDecomposition.volume_linear","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L74-L74","doc":"The linear volume law that the decomposition hypothesis delivers,\nvia Thurston additivity over the `Z + N` pieces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.AtomicJSJDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.AtomicJSJDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.AtomicJSJDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.AtomicJSJDecomposition","kind":"class","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L61-L75","doc":"**The decomposition hypothesis** (conjectural; `conj:jsj-decomposition-linearity`).\n\nThe atomic knot complement `𝒦(Z,N)` JSJ-decomposes along the\ninter-nucleon essential tori into exactly `Z` proton pieces and `N`\nneutron pieces, each carrying an isotope-independent volume quantum.\nGiven Thurston's additivity over the pieces, this yields the linear law.\n\nThis is the *open* part. It is a primary conjecture carrier: it takes no\nother conjecture class as a hypothesis, and **no instance is provided**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.Vol_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.Vol_n","kind":"opaque","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.Vol_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.Vol_p","kind":"opaque","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L23-L28","doc":"The foundational topological volume quanta for the QOU nucleon blocks.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.Vol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.Vol","kind":"opaque","line":15,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L15-L21","doc":"Axiomatization of the hyperbolic volume of a knot complement\n(Gromov norm / Thurston's volume).\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsKnots.AtomicKnot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsKnots.AtomicKnot","kind":"opaque","line":6,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsKnots/LinearJSJVolume.lean#L6-L13","doc":"An opaque type representing the knot complement of an isotope `(Z, N)`.\n(Postulated — the construction lives in the categorical substrate.)\n","signatureChunk":0}]}